{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPlan-review criterion prompts ship with no behavioral regression oracle. Of the 50\nplan-review criteria returned by `criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')`,\nonly 12 have an eval spec across `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` and `.rebar/evals/`. A\ncontributor editing any of the other rubrics under `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/` learns\nnothing if the edit reintroduces a false positive or drops a catch the criterion used to\nmake. ADR 0109 delivered a way to MEASURE a proposed change (the three-tier replay\nharness); it did not deliver an assertion of any criterion's required behavior on concrete\nmaterial.\n\nThe material for that assertion already exists and costs nothing to read. The committed\nmanifest `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-2026-08-30.manifest.json` records\n6,482 plan-review sidecar rows with `verified_count` 6,202 (`verified_ratio` 0.9568), and\n`plan_replay/corpus.py` reconstructs each row's at-review plan text. `sidecar.py:650-716`\nretains, per finding, the `criteria` list, `cohort` (`sidecar.py:667-672`), `norm_id`,\n`decision`, and `decision_margin` — enough to state, for a real plan, which criteria fired,\nand — via the per-finding `cohort` set — which criteria were routed for that plan yet\nproduced no finding (silence that is evidence, not mere absence).\n\n## Approach\n\nMine that corpus offline into per-criterion fire/no-fire eval fixtures on real plans, and\nadmit a fixture only after it reproduces against current code.\n\n**No-fire evidence predicate.** The sidecar persists only findings that FIRED, so a\ncriterion's silence on a plan is an ABSENCE inference and is never, on its own, a valid\n`expect: pass` case: silence because chunking never routed the criterion to that plan is\nindistinguishable from silence because the criterion correctly found nothing. The selector\ntherefore admits a plan as no-fire evidence for criterion C only when C is present in the\n`cohort` set of at least one finding recorded for that plan (`sidecar.py:667-672` — the\nsorted criterion-id set co-resident in the finder call that produced the finding, proving C\nwas routed/evaluated) AND no finding recorded for that plan cites C. A row whose `cohort`\nkey is MISSING is treated as unknown and skipped as a no-fire candidate — never emitted as\n`expect: pass` — exactly as the sidecar's own contract mandates (\"offline analysis MUST\ntreat a MISSING cohort as unknown (skip it), never as an empty set\"). Reproduction consensus\nin the no-fire direction ranges over the equal-`material_fingerprint` reviews satisfying\nthis predicate; the selector owns it and the emitter transcribes it.\n\nThis fits because the fixture is the artifact the existing machinery already consumes:\n`rebar criteria eval` runs a criterion's cases through its real Pass-1 finder\n(`eval_solver.py:139-142`), and `.rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` is an established,\nvalidated seam (`eval.py:69-78`). A fixture therefore adds zero production tokens, cannot\nbias a live review, and composes with the ADR 0109 harness rather than duplicating it.\n\nThis epic REPLACES its own earlier R-4 framing (per-criterion worked examples injected into\nreviewer prompts). Two mechanical facts in this codebase decided it: the Pass-1 rubric is\nassembled into `instructions` at `passes.py:284,292-297`, AFTER the cache breakpoint set at\n`passes.py:291`, so prompt-resident examples are re-billed on every chunk of every review\nin perpetuity; and an observed false positive used both as a prompt example and as an eval\ncase makes the eval measure nothing.\n\n## Scope\n\nChildren covering, in dependency order: budget-cap parameterization of the eval ledger; the\noffline candidate selector; the spec emitter; the admission runner and its drift report;\nchange-triggered execution; the gap-only self-healing loop; and the protocol ADR plus docs.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Injecting anything into reviewer prompts. No file under `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/`\n  changes in this epic.\n- Fixtures for criteria that already have a spec. `eval.py:69-78` resolves a project spec\n  as a REPLACEMENT for the packaged one, so writing one there would delete the packaged\n  cases.\n- Shipping rebar's fixtures as packaged core for other projects. The tooling is the reusable\n  artifact; a project overriding criteria owns its own evals, as it already owns its tests.\n- Closing the drift the admission run discovers. Each entry becomes a follow-on ticket\n  linked `discovered_from` this epic.\n- Per-finding true/false-positive labelling or human adjudication. The 2026-07-16 attempt\n  was invalidated at ~79% contaminated labels and descoped\n  (`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/README.md:112-118`); it is not retried here.\n- Restructuring the prompt cache so eval prefixes become cacheable.\n\n## Budget\n\nEpic ceiling **$450** including a $75 reserve, enforced by the parameterized ledger and\nallocated per child: ledger $0, selector $0, emitter $0, admission runner $250,\nchange-triggered execution $25, self-healing loop $100, ADR/docs $0. The admission bootstrap\ncentral estimate is $112 (22 criteria at the 1-TURN/2-STEP rate x 24 calls x $0.03, plus 16\nAGENT criteria x 24 x $0.25), band $68-$229, using the per-call rates evidenced by\n`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl`. Steady-state cost after this epic\nis zero unless a rubric changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A no-fire (`expect: pass`) case is emitted for criterion C on a plan only when C is\n      present in the `cohort` set of some finding recorded for that plan AND no finding on\n      that plan cites C; a row with a missing `cohort` key is skipped, never emitted as\n      `expect: pass`; verified by `pytest` over a synthetic corpus holding one in-cohort\n      silent plan (emitted), one plan where C was never in cohort (skipped), and one row\n      with a missing cohort key (skipped).\n- [ ] Every plan-review criterion that `criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')`\n      reports and that had no eval spec when this epic opened either has a spec file under\n      `.rebar/evals/`, or an open ticket titled `unreliable-criterion: <criterion-id>`\n      recording why it has none; verified by a script that sets the routing key set against\n      `ls .rebar/evals/ src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` and the open-ticket titles, and exits\n      non-zero if any criterion is in neither set.\n- [ ] No fixture enters `.rebar/evals/` without having reproduced against current code, and\n      the candidates that failed to reproduce are recorded with both their historical and\n      observed behavior; verified by the committed drift report plus the admission run's\n      admitted/withheld counts.\n- [ ] A criterion's fixtures execute when that criterion's rubric file changes, and the\n      criteria covered by this epic do not join the existing weekly live sweep; verified by\n      `grep` of the resolved weekly spec list showing none of the new prompt ids.\n- [ ] A run whose pre-flight estimate would exceed the epic ceiling is refused before it\n      issues any model call; verified by `pytest` over the ledger refusal test.\n- [ ] No file under `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/` is modified by this epic; verified by\n      `git diff --stat origin/main..HEAD -- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/` producing no output.\n- [ ] The mining and admission protocol is recorded as an ADR under `docs/adr/` and\n      referenced from `docs/plan-review-gate.md`; verified by `grep -q` for the ADR filename\n      in `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n\n## Child decomposition\n\nEach acceptance criterion above is owned by at least one child, non-overlapping:\n\n- No-fire predicate AC -> the selector (owns and applies the cohort/no-finding predicate)\n  and the emitter (transcribes the recorded no-fire candidates into `expect: pass` cases).\n- Coverage AC -> the selector (which candidates are trustworthy evidence), the emitter\n  (which turns them into validated specs) and the admission runner (which writes the\n  surviving ones), with residual gaps handled by the self-healing loop, which files the\n  `unreliable-criterion:` tickets.\n- Reproduction/drift AC -> the admission runner.\n- Change-triggered execution AC -> the change-triggered execution child.\n- Budget-refusal AC -> the ledger parameterization child, consumed by the admission runner.\n- Untouched-prompts AC -> a constraint on every child; no child edits a rubric.\n- ADR AC -> the ADR and docs child.\n\nOrdering edges: the selector precedes the emitter, and the emitter and the ledger\nparameterization both precede the admission runner; the admission runner precedes\nchange-triggered execution and the self-healing loop; the ADR child records the protocol the\nothers implement and lands last."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788386480017427669,"uuid":"5f8f43d5-f442-4168-bf29-b397197ee070"}